# Draft knowledge entry: eigenpy can use a pinned NumPy wheel for compile-time headers
id: DRAFT-eigenpy-numpy-header-wheel-fallback
trigger_tool: conan|python|cmake
phase: build|configure
error_signature: "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'numpy'|numpy.get_include|NUMPY_INCLUDE_DIRS|arrayobject.h"

severity: 2
category: eigenpy|numpy|ohos|headers|cmake
match_keywords: eigenpy, NumPy headers, numpy.get_include, ModuleNotFoundError, Python3_NumPy_INCLUDE_DIRS, arrayobject.h

title: eigenpy can fall back to a pinned NumPy wheel for compile-time headers
root_cause: >
  eigenpy requires NumPy's generated C headers to compile, but official OHOS CI
  workers may have CPython headers and libpython without an installed numpy
  module for the selected interpreter. Directly importing numpy in the recipe or
  in jrl-cmakemodules then fails before configure, even though the build only
  needs the include directory at that point.
affected_scope: >
  eigenpy 3.13.0 OHOS recipes and similar Boost.Python/NumPy extension builds
  where runtime NumPy is optional for CI artifact validation but NumPy C headers
  are required at compile time.
verification_cmd: |
  conan source archives/e/eigenpy/3.13.0
  conan export archives/e/eigenpy/3.13.0 --user=ohpcd --channel=stable
  sh "$HOME/bin/run-ohos-shadow-ci.sh" archives/e/eigenpy/3.13.0

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: import-first-then-pinned-header-wheel
rec_description: >
  First ask the selected interpreter for numpy.get_include(). If that import
  fails, extract a pinned CPython 3.12 aarch64 NumPy wheel during source() and
  use only numpy/_core/include as the compile-time header root. Prepend a tiny
  configure-only numpy stub to PYTHONPATH for CMake's get_include/version probes.
rec_command: |
  PYTHONPATH=<build>/numpy-stub cmake ... -DNUMPY_INCLUDE_DIRS=<wheel>/numpy/_core/include
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: ohos-numpy-header-wheel-fallback

fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: static-elf-test-when-runtime-numpy-is-missing
fallback_description: >
  If the build used vendored headers but the CI worker still lacks runtime
  NumPy during test_package import, run the C++ consumer smoke test and then
  verify eigenpy_pywrap as a valid ELF extension with sane NEEDED entries.
fallback_command: |
  llvm-readelf -d <installed eigenpy_pywrap>
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: ohos-missing-runtime-numpy-elf-fallback

forbid_1_pattern: "import numpy.*raise ConanInvalidConfiguration"
forbid_1_reason: Missing runtime NumPy should not block configure when generated headers are available from a pinned wheel.
forbid_1_consequence: Official CI workers without numpy fail before CMake configure.

principles: import-real-numpy-first, use-headers-only-from-wheel, do-not-package-wheel-runtime
source_event: eigenpy/3.13.0 official CI #34221 missing runtime NumPy
last_updated: 2026-08-29
